// =============================================================================
// pigemma-probe (tools/probe/probe.cpp) - the one custom llama.cpp program of
// the pi-gemma4 experiment: a cb_eval recorder with three modes.
//
//   names      print every graph tensor name seen by the eval callback (sorted,
//              unique, one per line) to stdout. Used to verify the tensor-name
//              contract (docs/TRACE_FORMAT.md section 6).
//   moe-trace  record, per processed token and MoE layer, the K selected
//              experts (ffn_moe_topk, a strided I32 view of the argsort) and
//              their renormalised routing weights (ffn_moe_weights_norm), plus
//              optionally the top-P router probabilities (ffn_moe_probs), into
//              a .moetrace file (docs/TRACE_FORMAT.md section 3) with the
//              sidecars <trace>.tokens.bin and <trace>.gen.txt.
//   act-dump   dump fp16 activations of chosen layers/kinds (default ffn_norm,
//              ffn_geglu, ffn_out = the inputs/outputs of the dense FFN
//              matrices) as L<il>.<kind>.npy with a fixed 128-byte header, plus
//              phase.u8, tokens.bin and meta.json (section 7). Input of H2.
//
// Input is one of: -p/-f text (tokenised once, split into fresh-context chunks
// of --chunk-tokens, BOS inserted at the start of every chunk), --gen-prompts
// FILE.json (one chunk per prompt), or --replay tokens.bin (teacher-forced
// replay of an i32 stream, e.g. <trace>.tokens.bin). After each chunk's
// prefill the probe can generate greedily (--gen N); generated tokens are
// recorded with phase 1. Every chunk starts from an empty KV cache
// (llama_memory_clear), so `pos` restarts at 0.
//
// On Linux --io-csv F writes one row per ubatch (with -ub 1: per token):
// token_index,phase,wall_ms,read_bytes_delta,majflt_delta,rss_anon_kb,rss_file_kb
// from /proc/self/io, /proc/self/stat (field 12) and /proc/self/status. The
// row boundary is the eval callback on the graph's last node "result_output";
// if that node is not observed, a residual row is written after llama_process.
//
// All standard llama.cpp COMMON arguments work (-m -f -p -t -tb -c -b -ub -nr
// -lm -ctk -ctv -fa ...); probe flags are removed from argv before
// common_params_parse(..., LLAMA_EXAMPLE_COMMON). `--help` prints a 3-line
// banner, the llama.cpp help, then the PIGEMMA section.
//
// Exit codes: 0 ok; 2 usage error; 3 load / compute / output-file failure;
// 4 tensor contract violation (wrong type/shape, missing or extra columns,
// model without experts in moe-trace); 128+signal (130 SIGINT, 143 SIGTERM)
// when interrupted - outputs are still closed cleanly. One line
// "PIGEMMA_SUMMARY {json}" is written to stderr at exit (also on errors) with
// the TRACE_FORMAT 4.5 keys (mode, exit_code, n_prompt, n_gen, n_records,
// n_chunks, t_load_ms, t_p_eval_ms, t_eval_ms, tok_s_prompt, tok_s_gen,
// callback_ms, trace_out, act_out, io_csv) plus n_p_eval, n_eval,
// t_prefill_wall_ms, t_gen_wall_ms, wall_tok_s_prompt, wall_tok_s_gen (probe
// wall clock around the decode calls, incl. callback overhead - a separate
// source from llama_perf), wall_ms, n_ctx, n_threads, interrupted, error,
// probe_version, llama_build, llama_commit.
//
// Mandatory llama settings (applied by the probe, not by the caller):
//   params.warmup = false   (warm-up routes every token to ALL experts,
//                            src/llama-graph.cpp:1473, polluting the trace)
//   params.cb_eval / cb_eval_user_data = the recorder
//   params.sampling.backend_sampling = false (logits must stay on the host)
//
// Build (out-of-tree, tools/CMakeLists.txt; links llama-common + llama like
// examples/eval-callback). Docker (desktop):
//   cmake -S /work/tools -B /work/tools/build-linux-x86 -G Ninja
//         -DLLAMA_DIR=/work/third_party/llama.cpp -DGGML_NATIVE=OFF -DGGML_AVX2=ON
//         -DGGML_AVX512=ON -DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=Release        (one command line)
//   cmake --build /work/tools/build-linux-x86 --target pigemma-probe
// Pi: the same with -DGGML_NATIVE=ON (see tools/CMakeLists.txt header).
//
// Documented decisions / deviations from the manifest text (also reported as
// open issues):
//  D-a --chat uses the model's own chat template by default (GGUF
//      tokenizer.chat_template rendered through llama.cpp's common_chat
//      templates, thinking disabled). The manifest's literal
//      "<start_of_turn>user\n...<end_of_turn>\n<start_of_turn>model\n" is NOT
//      the Gemma 4 format: the Gemma 4 vocab has no <start_of_turn> token
//      (verified in the 26B GGUF: <|turn> = 105, <turn|> = 106). It is kept
//      as --chat-style gemma3; --chat-style gemma4 is the built-in literal
//      "<|turn>user\n...<turn|>\n<|turn>model\n<|channel>thought\n<channel|>",
//      also the fallback when the template cannot be rendered.
//  D-b Raw -p/-f text is tokenised as literal text (parse_special = false)
//      so corpus code/text containing marker-like strings is not turned into
//      control tokens; --parse-special restores llama.cpp's default. Chat
//      wrapping always parses specials (the markers must become tokens).
//  D-c --tokens T applies to every mode (stop after T recorded tokens,
//      prefill + generated; it is also the act-dump npy T_MAX, default 512)
//      and --max-chunks N limits the number of chunks; the 72-token smoke
//      trace is `--chunk-tokens 64 --gen 8 --tokens 72`.
//  D-d A chunk longer than n_batch is decoded as consecutive sub-batches of
//      n_batch tokens (llama_batch_ext capacity is n_batch); the manifest
//      assumes n_batch >= chunk. Columns still accumulate in token order.
//  D-e When -c is absent the probe sets n_ctx = max(4096, chunk_tokens +
//      max generation + 8, rounded up to 256) instead of the model's 262144
//      training context. An explicit `-c 0` is respected.
//  D-f Replay never inserts BOS (the replayed stream must stay identical to
//      the source stream: replay token_index i == source token A+i); use
//      --replay-chunks <src>.meta.json to cut at the source chunk starts.
//      --gen is ignored in replay (every replay record is phase 0).
//  D-g moe_layers = the layers that emitted ffn_moe_topk in the first chunk;
//      the .moetrace header is therefore written when the first chunk's
//      records are flushed (allowed by TRACE_FORMAT 3.4), with the 16 KiB
//      header reserve, and patched at close (n_records written last).
//  D-h I/O errors on the output files exit 3 (runtime failure); the manifest
//      lists 3 as "load/compute failure" only.
// =============================================================================

